invariant: INV-13
file: tls_write.c
catches: unit
reason: a KeyUpdate that ch_write could not send fails the session with
  unexpected_message, which says the peer sent a message out of order,
  where the failure is this side's own send. bin/unit has the peer ask for
  a KeyUpdate, fails the send of the answer the next ch_write owes, and
  requires internal_error from ch_alert_sent.

--- old
    int rc = hspost_send_key_update(t);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        tlsi_fail(t, ALERT_INTERNAL_ERROR);
    }
--- new
    int rc = hspost_send_key_update(t);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        tlsi_fail(t, ALERT_UNEXPECTED_MESSAGE);
    }
